From 9ddff7a23481832552393e56a22fe36cd864b022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:18:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ncz: suppress the hot corner hint badge

Downstream aesthetic choice: the corner hint ("Overview  Super+Space") is not
shown in NCZ.

It sits on GtkLayerShell.Layer.OVERLAY while the app chooser is on TOP, and
zwlr_layer_shell orders background < bottom < top < overlay, so it always
composites above the chooser. The badge is only cleared by on_leave(), and
triggering a hot corner means the pointer is in the corner and usually stays
there while the user looks at what opened -- so it sits over the UI it just
launched. Reproduced identically on a 1080p panel and a 4K panel, which is what
ruled out a scaling or timing explanation.

Hot corner behaviour is untouched: corners still arm and still fire their
action. Only the badge is suppressed.

Reported upstream as singularityos-lab/singularity-shell#19, where the
suggested fix is to hide the hint when its action fires rather than waiting for
pointer-leave. If that lands, this patch can be dropped.
---
 src/core/hot_corner_manager.vala | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/hot_corner_manager.vala b/src/core/hot_corner_manager.vala
index 44f182c..ce51caa 100644
--- a/src/core/hot_corner_manager.vala
+++ b/src/core/hot_corner_manager.vala
@@ -108,6 +108,20 @@ namespace Singularity {
         }
 
         private void show_hint(int corner, string? action) {
+            // NCZ: the corner hint badge is suppressed downstream as an
+            // aesthetic choice.
+            //
+            // It lives on GtkLayerShell.Layer.OVERLAY while the app chooser is
+            // on TOP, so it draws above the chooser it just opened: the pointer
+            // is still inside the corner region at that moment, and the hint
+            // only clears on on_leave(), so it sits over the UI the user is now
+            // looking at.
+            //
+            // Hot corner behaviour is untouched -- the corner still arms and
+            // still fires its action; only the badge is hidden.
+            hide_hints();
+            if (true) return;
+
             if (corner < 0 || action == null) {
                 hide_hints();
                 return;
